-- title:
--   Finiteness of residue fields of finite-type algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring and $\mathfrak m \subseteq A$ a maximal ideal whose residue ring $A/\mathfrak m$ is finite. Let $B$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $A$-algebra structure which is of finite type over $A$, i.e. $B$ is generated as an $A$-algebra by finitely many elements, and let $\mathfrak p \subseteq B$ be a maximal ideal. Assume that the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m$ under the structure map $A \to B$ is contained in $\mathfrak p$, i.e. $\mathrm{Ideal.map}\ (\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A\ B)\ \mathfrak m \le \mathfrak p$. The conclusion is that the quotient $B/\mathfrak p$ is a finite type, i.e. the residue field of $B$ at $\mathfrak p$ is a finite set. No Noetherian, reducedness or flatness hypothesis is imposed on $A$ or $B$; finiteness of $A/\mathfrak m$ and the finite-type condition are all that is used.
--
--   This is Zariski's lemma (the weak Nullstellensatz) in the form: a residue field at a closed point of a finite-type algebra over a point with finite residue field is again finite. It is used, for instance, with $A$ a discrete valuation ring with finite residue field and $B$ a moduli ring of finite type, to see that closed points of the special fibre have finite residue fields, and hence in the study of adic completions of such moduli rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_finite_quotient_of_isMaximal_of_finiteType_of_finite_quotient.lean

